doctype html
html(lang='en')
  head
    title FISH Disconnect Handling Explained
    style.
        dd {
            margin-left: 2em;
        }
  body
    h2 FISH DISCONNECT HANDLING
    p.
        Participants sometimes lose their connection during a game: the page is reloaded,
        the phone's screen locks, someone switches to another app, or the signal drops.
        When this feature is off, a participant whose connection drops after the game has
        started is removed at once, and the rest of the group plays on without them.
    p.
        When it is on, a disconnected participant stays in the game for a grace period.
        If they open the game again in that time (with the same experiment code and
        participant ID), they go straight back into the current season with their catch
        and profit intact, without seeing the rules again.
    p.
        A disconnected participant's boat is sent back to port, so they don't keep paying
        for time at sea while they are away.
    h4 Settings
    dl
        dt Grace period to reconnect (seconds)
        dd.
            How long a disconnected participant has to come back. If the game pauses,
            the other players wait this long, so keep it short; 30 seconds is the default.
        dt During the grace period
        dd.
            <b>Pause game:</b> the game stops for everyone, and the other players see
            "A player has lost their connection. Waiting for them to return" with a countdown.
            When the pause ends, everyone sees "the game resumes in N s" before play
            continues; N is the initial delay, but at least 2 and at most 5 seconds.
            <br/>
            <b>Continue game:</b> the game goes on and the other players are not told.
            The absent participant catches nothing while they are away, which may affect
            the group's results.
        dt Disconnects allowed per participant
        dd.
            How many times each participant may disconnect. The next disconnect after
            that counts as lost straight away, with no grace period. This stops one
            unreliable connection from holding up the group again and again.
        dt When a participant is lost
        dd.
            A participant is lost when the grace period runs out, or when they go over
            the disconnects allowed.
            <br/>
            <b>End and record the game:</b> the game ends for everyone, the other players
            see a message saying a player lost their connection, and the run is saved
            with the reason recorded.
            <br/>
            <b>Remove them and play on:</b> the others carry on without them, as when
            the feature is off.
    p.
        A participant who has been lost cannot rejoin that game, and is not placed in
        a new group either.
    h4 In the results
    p.
        Every disconnect, return, removal and game end is saved with the run, with the
        season and second it happened in. This also happens when the feature is off.
        The CSV export has four columns for it. The first three are per season: a
        disconnect during the break between seasons counts toward the season that follows.
    dl
        dt Disconnects
        dd How many times the participant's connection dropped in that season.
        dt Seconds Away
        dd Time away in that season, counting only the times they came back.
        dt Lost
        dd.
            Whether and why the participant was lost in that season, for example
            "removed: grace period expired".
        dt Run End Reason
        dd.
            Why the run ended: time (all seasons played), depletion (no fish left),
            nohumans (all participants gone), or disconnect (a lost participant ended it).
